import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"Retro — the meta-arena player (Q3, first answer)","description":"","frontmatter":{"title":"Retro — the meta-arena player (Q3, first answer)","type":"retro","date":"2026-10-14T00:00:00.000Z"},"headers":[],"relativePath":"graphopt/project/retros/meta-arena-player.md","filePath":"vendored/graphopt/project/retros/meta-arena-player.md"}`),a={name:`graphopt/project/retros/meta-arena-player.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="retro-—-the-meta-arena-player-q3-first-answer" tabindex="-1">Retro — the meta-arena player (Q3, first answer) <a class="header-anchor" href="#retro-—-the-meta-arena-player-q3-first-answer" aria-label="Permalink to “Retro — the meta-arena player (Q3, first answer)”">​</a></h1><p>Plan 0021&#39;s Q3: is the mixed board deep enough that a <em>learned</em> player beats the scripted <code>saturate → extract</code> playbook? The machinery is landed — <code>catopt_discovery.meta_player</code> is a linear softmax policy over <code>meta_arena.legal_actions</code> with an exact (uncapped) softmax, played-move masking, ε-exploration, and reward-to-go REINFORCE; the schema is data (<code>lawdata.META_ARENA_FEATURES</code>). Reproduce:</p><pre><code>.venv/bin/python -m catopt_discovery.meta_player \\
    --train-cases 1000 --eval-cases 20 --budget 24 \\
    --temperature 1.2 --epsilon 0.25 --json run.json
</code></pre><h2 id="the-paying-line-exists-—-verified-by-hand" tabindex="-1">The paying line exists — verified by hand <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-paying-line-exists-—-verified-by-hand" aria-label="Permalink to “The paying line exists — verified by hand”">​</a></h2><p>The Q2 probe&#39;s baseline table already showed the headroom: scripted/greedy/random all tie at baseline on every demo case. What they miss is a <em>four-move composition</em>: <code>declare</code> a fresh fold of a mined spec → <code>saturate</code> so the minted rule fires → <code>handle</code> to bind a supported kernel → <code>extract</code> to collect. Hand-set weights prove the schema expresses it: silu sites go 2→1, swiglu 3→1, nested 4→3, controls and infeasible-kernel boards correctly decline. <code>test_winning_line_reachable</code> pins it.</p><h2 id="the-measurement-—-cold-rl-does-not-find-it-at-1000-episodes" tabindex="-1">The measurement — cold RL does not find it (at 1000 episodes) <a class="header-anchor" href="#the-measurement-—-cold-rl-does-not-find-it-at-1000-episodes" aria-label="Permalink to “The measurement — cold RL does not find it (at 1000 episodes)”">​</a></h2><p><code>gen_cases</code> mixes paying boards (silu/swiglu sites under <code>sans = DEFAULT - {silu_fold, softsign_fold}</code>, kernel still in the ambient vocabulary) with non-paying ones (softsign under <code>sans</code> — kernel out of vocab; controls under <code>DEFAULT</code>).</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>player</th><th style="text-align:right;">reward</th><th style="text-align:right;">cert</th><th style="text-align:right;">decl</th><th style="text-align:right;">steps</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>scripted</td><td style="text-align:right;">−0.10</td><td style="text-align:right;">20</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">2.0</td></tr><tr><td>greedy</td><td style="text-align:right;">−1.20</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">24.0 (drain)</td></tr><tr><td>random</td><td style="text-align:right;">−1.09</td><td style="text-align:right;">5</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">21.7</td></tr><tr><td>learned</td><td style="text-align:right;"><strong>−0.07</strong></td><td style="text-align:right;">20</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">1.4</td></tr><tr><td>learned-greedy</td><td style="text-align:right;">−0.05</td><td style="text-align:right;">20</td><td style="text-align:right;">0</td><td style="text-align:right;">1.0</td></tr></tbody></table><p>Train decade means climb steadily (−0.94 → −0.41, plateau ~−0.44) — the learner is doing real work: <code>op:extract</code> +3.47, <code>op:fire</code> −2.54. What it converged to is the <em>stoppable-time</em> policy: extract immediately, skip the wasteful saturate. That honestly beats scripted on mean reward — but on declared-use columns it wins nothing.</p><h2 id="why-the-line-is-hard-—-and-what-this-measures" tabindex="-1">Why the line is hard — and what this measures <a class="header-anchor" href="#why-the-line-is-hard-—-and-what-this-measures" aria-label="Permalink to “Why the line is hard — and what this measures”">​</a></h2><p>The net payout for the composed line is ~+0.25 over immediate-extract; per-step cost −0.05 makes the margin thin, and on 3/5 board kinds the line does not exist at all — a policy that learns &quot;declare usually doesn&#39;t pay&quot; is <em>locally correct</em>. This is the sparse-reward credit-assignment wall: the memoryless linear policy cannot plan a composition. Two features were added on the way and confirmed load-bearing-weak: <code>st:unhandled</code>/<code>x:unhandled:handle</code> (declared-but-unhandled is exactly where <code>handle</code> pays) and <code>st:handleable</code>/<code>x:handleable: declare</code> (a mined spec whose canon form a handler covers — the precondition, computable from <code>MetaState</code> data alone).</p><h2 id="verdict-and-next-levers" tabindex="-1">Verdict and next levers <a class="header-anchor" href="#verdict-and-next-levers" aria-label="Permalink to “Verdict and next levers”">​</a></h2><p><strong>Q3 is answered in the negative at this budget</strong>: a cold-start linear REINFORCE policy beats the scripted baseline on reward but only via the degenerate line — the composed strategy is in the policy class (hand weights reach it) yet unreachable by sampling at ~10³ episodes. The construction-arena result transfers: learning beat baselines where paying moves were dense; here they are composed, and composition is what the policy lacks.</p><p>Levers, in order of how well they match the tower&#39;s own thesis:</p><ol><li><s><strong>Options/macros</strong></s> — <strong>landed.</strong> <code>claim(tag)</code> is the composed line as one refereed move (declare a covered spec → fire its rule → bind the interpretation; Sanada&#39;s <code>handle (declare spec) with H</code> fused). With it in the legal set the line compresses to <code>claim → extract</code>: <em>sampling reachability is fixed</em> — the 300-episode run found 4 structural wins (silu 2→1) where zero existed before. Final reading — 800-episode run over occurrence-gated claims: <strong>learned −0.03 mean reward, 3 certified structural wins on 40 held-out cases (swiglu 3→1, silu 2→1, swiglu 3→2) — beats scripted (−0.10, zero structural wins) on both axes.</strong> <strong>Caveat: the wins ride sampling variance, not learned preference</strong> — <code>op:claim</code>&#39;s weight sits ≈+0.04, <code>learned-greedy</code> never claims. The board question is answered: a learned player beats scripted on the mixed board, <em>because the option move compressed the composition</em> — action-space structure is what the board was missing; consolidation by a memoryless linear policy remains the open gap for a stronger policy class.</li><li><s><strong>Curriculum</strong></s> — <strong>partially landed.</strong> Training on the paying-board subset (<code>claimable &gt; 0</code>; 250 of 400 generated) shifts the policy measurably: the stochastic arm&#39;s eval declared-wins tripled (9 of 40 incl. swiglu/silu sites and a <code>control</code> board with a paying subterm), mean cost 2.73 &lt; scripted&#39;s 2.92 — but mean reward degrades (−0.35) because the policy over-claims where the extraction then can&#39;t improve. Curriculum concentrates the gradient on the interesting boards; it does not teach <em>when to stop</em>.</li><li><strong>Imitation warm-start</strong> — behavior-clone the known line, then RL. Honest about which part is discovery vs consolidation.</li><li>More training — 10⁴+ episodes; the decade trend was still rising at plateau&#39;s edge.</li></ol><h2 id="housekeeping" tabindex="-1">Housekeeping <a class="header-anchor" href="#housekeeping" aria-label="Permalink to “Housekeeping”">​</a></h2><ul><li><code>lawdata.META_ARENA_PLAYER_WEIGHTS</code> stays empty — no trained snapshot ships until one earns it (the eval arms re-train in <code>main</code>; nothing memorized).</li><li>The ε knob and reward-to-go are <em>learner</em> machinery, not board changes — the reward table is untouched.</li></ul>`,17)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};